OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Tue 11 Aug to Thu 20 AugFA
OL,6,Fsettled start, with mainly dry
OL,7,Fconditions on Tuesday, although with
OL,8,Fscattered showers across western
OL,9,Fareas. Then through the week, more
OL,10,Fchangeable conditions are likely
OL,11,Facross northern parts, with some
OL,12,Fspells of rain or showers and stronger
OL,13,Fwinds, interspersed by drier periods.
OL,14,FWhilst southern areas will generally
OL,15,Fsee more settled, drier conditions
OL,16,Fwhere it will become very warm or hot.
OL,17,FFurther into August, lower pressure
OL,18,Fmay start to track further south or
OL,19,Feast. This means there is a greater
OL,20,Fchance of frontal systems or thundery
OL,21,Finterludes to affect southern and
OL,22,Feastern areas in comparison to recent
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,23,Fweeks, though rainfall amounts could
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
OL,24,Fbe quite variable with some areas
OL,25,Fstill seeing relatively little.
OL,26,FTemperatures look to remain above
FL,164,160,301,260,100,100
